+++
title: Egyptian mythology
hook: Few complete Egyptian myths appear anywhere in the sources. Most texts
  contain nothing more than allusions, or tell only portions of a larger
  story, and for any given myth the Egyptians themselves may have had only the
  general outlines.
standfirst: The myths of ancient Egypt describe the actions of the gods as a
  means of understanding the world, and the beliefs they express are an
  important part of Egyptian religion. They appear in short stories, hymns,
  ritual and funerary texts and temple decoration, rarely as a complete
  account.
