  model: claude-opus-5
  left-out: The heading "Influence in Egyptian culture" has no prose of its own
    in the source — the article goes straight from it to "In religion" — so
    its body is empty rather than invented; the heading is kept because no
    section may be dropped. The article's footnote numbering has gaps (nothing
    between ^42 and ^52, and no ^80 between ^79 and ^81); I carried the
    numbers exactly as they appear rather than renumbering. The image
    Flickr_-_Gaspa_-_Dendara,_tempio_di_Hator_(56).jpg is listed in the front
    matter but has no figure in the prose, so I placed it in "Osiris myth",
    the section its front-matter caption describes. The Wikidata image claim
    points at Great_Sphinx_of_Giza_May_2015.JPG, which is not among the
    article's images and is not described anywhere in the prose, so it is not
    in the image plan. Three figure captions carry the footnote references
    they had in the source (^27, ^97, ^107); the other captions had none.
    Caption wording is plain text rather than MDY, so the links that the
    source's figcaptions carried (Ra, barque, Mesektet Barque, Set (deity),
    Apophis, underworld, Egyptian Museum, Cairo, solar barque) appear as words
    only. No ancient-source quotations exist in the article, so the
    pull-quotes are the three modern scholarly quotations it contains.
